islative_action","historyId":"118201634","location":"Senate","sequence":23,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"In Senate. Concurrence in Assembly amendments pending.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-concurred","code":null,"date":"2025-09-10","eventType":"concurred","historyId":"118201635","location":"Senate","sequence":24,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Assembly amendments concurred in. (Ayes 40. Noes 0. Page 2829.) Ordered to engrossing and enrolling.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-enrolled","code":null,"date":"2025-09-17","eventType":"enrolled","historyId":"118201636","location":"Governor","sequence":25,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Enrolled and presented to the Governor at 2 p.m.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-approved","code":null,"date":"2025-10-02","eventType":"approved_by_governor","historyId":"118201637","location":"Governor","sequence":26,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Approved by the Governor.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-chaptered","code":null,"date":"2025-10-02","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"118201638","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":27,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State. Chapter 246, Statutes of 2025.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_ADDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Section 18107.5 is added to the Elections Code, to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2025-10-02","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 246, Statutes of 2025","number":"246","type":"CHP","year":"2025"},"chapteredDate":"2025-10-02","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"683dd7db074b59df30edee6adf1cb58a18c3b8231498e4e23b8f8fbe75d6c45f","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"Under existing law, it is a crime for a person to receive money or other valuable consideration to assist another to register to vote by receiving the completed affidavit of registration if the person fails to sign the affidavit and include certain other information, including the name and telephone number of the person, company, or organization, if any, that has agreed to pay the money or other valuable consideration.\n\nThis bill would make it a crime, punishable by a fine of up to $10,000, imprisonment for up to 3 years, or both, for a person to knowingly or willfully pay or offer to pay money or other valuable consideration to another person with the intent to induce the person to vote or to register to vote, or where the payment is contingent upon whether the person voted or the person’s voter registration status. By creating a new crime, this bill would impose a state-mandated local program.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that no reimbursement is required by this act for a specified reason.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-sb398","identifier":"SB 398","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"YES","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2025-02-14","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Election crimes: payment based on voting or voter registration.","ruleId":"tag-reg-1","tag":"registration"}],"judic